{"name":"Herb Garland","hex":"#64654a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"herb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant whose stem is not woody and does not persist beyond each growing season.","Grass; herbage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herb"},{"term":"garland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A circular or linear decoration, especially one of plaited flowers or leaves, worn on the body or draped as a decoration.","An accolade or mark of honour."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deck or ornament something with a garland.","To form something into a garland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garland"}],"entries":[{"title":"Herb","blocks":[{"text":"Herbs are a widely distributed and widespread group of plants, excluding vegetables, with savory or aromatic properties that are used for flavoring and garnishing food, for medicinal purposes, or for fragrances. Culinary use typically distinguishes herbs from spices. Herbs generally refers to the leafy green or flowering parts of a plant, while spices are usually dried and produced from other parts of the plant, including seeds, bark, roots and fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Garden_of_herbs.jpg/330px-Garden_of_herbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herb","wikidata":"Q207123"},{"title":"Garland","blocks":[{"text":"A garland is a decorative braid, knot or wreath of flowers, leaves, or other material. Garlands can be worn on the head or around the neck, hung on an inanimate object, or laid in a place of cultural or religious importance. In contemporary times, garlands are used to decorate, especially around holidays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Choinka.JPG/330px-Choinka.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w